From: John de Kroon
Subject: [PATCH] Saved games in the current directory, Backspace only deletes

The configuration and saved games went to /mnt/.fdoom.tar/, a fixed path
that an app may not reach: saving ended the game with an error. They now
go to the current directory, which doom makes APP_DATA. Backspace quit the
game at any moment, also while typing a save's name; it now reaches the
game, and Quit Game and the logo key end it.
---
--- a/fbdoom/i_input_tty.c
+++ b/fbdoom/i_input_tty.c
@@ -436,11 +436,6 @@
     
     while (kbd_read(&pressed, &key))
     {
-        if (key == 0x0E) {
-            kbd_shutdown();
-            I_Quit();
-        }
-
         UpdateShiftStatus(pressed, key);
 
         // process event
--- a/fbdoom/m_config.c
+++ b/fbdoom/m_config.c
@@ -2051,8 +2051,8 @@
     char *homedir;
     char *result;
 
-    // frosted HACK - homedir = getenv("HOME");
-    homedir = "/mnt";
+    /* the current directory, where doom starts us: APP_DATA */
+    return strdup("");
 
     if (homedir != NULL)
     {
